      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Let $r=\\,i+3j+4k$ and $s=3i-j.$ Find the vector projection of $r$ onto $s.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{s}\\,r=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{s}\\,r & =\\frac{r\\cdot s}{s\\cdot s}s \\\\  & =\\frac{{r}_{x}{s}_{x}+{r}_{y}{s}_{y}+{r}_{z}{s}_{z}}{{s}_{x}^{2}+{s}_{y}^{2}+{s}_{z}^{2}}s \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)\\cdot 3+(3)\\cdot (-1)+(4)\\cdot 0}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}s \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}s \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
